{
    "pageid": 888,
    "title": "Casus Belli modding",
    "sections": [
        {
            "heading": "Introduction",
            "level": 1,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Casus Belli are quite complex to mod, as lot of flags and scopes are involved."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "CB life-cycle is the following:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "When selecting a target character, can_use is evaluated",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "If character is eligible, can_use_title is evaluated on the titles in the realm (which titles are scanned depend on CB flags like check_all_titles , check_de_jure_tier ,...)",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "War is declared on the contested title (for AI this also depends on ai_will_do and some hardcoded logic)",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "on_add , on_add_title and on_add_posttitle are executed.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "During the duration of the war, is_valid and is_valid_title are regularly executed to ensure CB remains valid (otherwise war ends as inconclusive)",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Each battle and occupied holding contribute to warscore based on CB parameters. Depending on CB type, there might be an additional ticking warscore.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Depending on the output of the war either on_success , on_fail or on_reverse_demand and associated title/posttitle blocks are executed.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "A truce is applied between attacker and defender, whose duration depend on value of truce_days",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
