        {
            "heading": "Special symbols",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "In the war name and casus belli name, there are special hard-coded symbols available:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "table",
                    "rows": [
                        [
                            "Symbol",
                            "Example",
                            "Description"
                        ],
                        [
                            "$ORDER$",
                            "Second",
                            "An ordinal, based on how many times the title holder has used this cause for war.  On the first usage, the symbol evaluates to the blank string \"\".  Thereafter, it evaluates to the ordinal number of the war, like \"Second\", \"Third\", etc., with an added space.  This symbol should always be flush with the following text, e.g., \"The $ORDER$World War\", because it includes its own space only as needed."
                        ],
                        [
                            "$FIRST$",
                            "Kingdom of England",
                            "The name of the attacker's primary title (ROOT)"
                        ],
                        [
                            "$FIRST_ADJ$",
                            "English",
                            "The demonym (demographic adjective name) of the attacker (ROOT)"
                        ],
                        [
                            "$SECOND$",
                            "Kingdom of France",
                            "The name of the defender's primary title (FROM)"
                        ],
                        [
                            "$SECOND_ADJ$",
                            "French",
                            "The demonym (demographic adjective name) of the defender (FROM)"
                        ],
                        [
                            "$ATTACKER$",
                            "King Henry VI",
                            "The titled first name of the attacker (ROOT)"
                        ],
                        [
                            "$DEFENDER$",
                            "Jeanne d'Arc",
                            "The titled first name of the defender (FROM)"
                        ],
                        [
                            "$CLAIMANT$",
                            "Lisa Simpson",
                            "The titled first name of the claimant (FROMFROM)"
                        ],
                        [
                            "$OTHER_TITLE$",
                            "County of Orléans",
                            "The contested title in a claim war that targets a title."
                        ],
                        [
                            "$RELIGION$",
                            "Muslim",
                            "The adjective of the religion of the attacker (ROOT)"
                        ],
                        [
                            "$HOLY_WAR$",
                            "Fatwa",
                            "The holy war name as taken from the attacker's religion"
                        ]
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Bracketed commands",
            "level": 3,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Generally, vanilla avoids scoped bracketed localisation commands in all war names and casus belli keys.  Use of bracketed commands is mostly unsupported and there has been little research done in this area."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "However, the following special scopes are confirmed to have been used in vanilla casus belli:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "table",
                    "rows": [
                        [
                            "Scope",
                            "Description",
                            "Example Key",
                            "Example Text"
                        ],
                        [
                            "Actor",
                            "The attacker (ROOT)",
                            "WAR_NAME_HERETIC_UPRISING",
                            "$ORDER$$SECOND_ADJ$ [Actor.Religion.GetName] Revolt"
                        ],
                        [
                            "Title",
                            "The contested title in a claim war",
                            "WAR_NAME_LIBERATION_REVOLT",
                            "$ORDER$Liberation of [Title.GetBaseName]"
                        ],
                        [
                            "<offmap_power_name>",
                            "The name of an offmap power",
                            "WAR_NAME_INVASION_OF_CHINA",
                            "$ORDER$$FIRST_ADJ$ Invasion of the [offmap_china.GetFullName]\")"
                        ],
                        [
                            "Recipient",
                            "Designated heir ???",
                            "WAR_NAME_DISMANTLE_PRETENDER_CHINA",
                            "The $ORDER$[offmap_china.GetFullName] War to Dismantle the Pretender [Recipient.PrimaryTitle.GetFullName]"
                        ]
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
